3. Improved all-prime annihilator at the existing caller.
Let X be the actual nonzero Stickelberger integer for N,e>0.
Choose a from its first field. Write A0=a^e-1, B0=a^{e+1}-1,
X=A0 B0 b, with a>0 (prime-to-ell), hence natural subtractions
agree with their integer casts. In R=O/(ell^nu), let
S=sum_{u units} floorDiff a(u/(N ell^nu)) u^e psi(u).
The second field supplies one w for BOTH levels n and n-1.
For n>0 the exact power-sum decomposition is T_n=U_n+
ell^e psi(ell) T_{n-1}. Negation of unit residues changes the
weight sign modulo ell^n, so S=2U_n. Subtraction of the two
congruences gives (1-ell^e psi(ell))B0 X=w S. The factor
1-ell^e psi(ell) is a unit by finite geometric sum (e>0);
thus S divides B0 X. This also holds at n=0 in the zero ring.
This is the actual floor-sum lemma, not a new analytic premise.
For q split in Q(mu_{N ell^nu}), take the actual Jacobi family
at 1/(N ell^nu): it is fixed by H, a unit off q, and its
conjugate orders are floorDiff a. Apply (A) with r=1 in the
off-q alternative. S A0 x(phi)=0. If B0 X=k S, multiply
